  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 102 AM MST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nIt seems like winds may stay a little too high Monday night for\nanother round of fog and low clouds to form, but will have to\nwatch for this anywhere winds fully diminish. Temperatures will \nbe chilly Monday night, though not the coldest we've seen this \nseason.\n\nShortwave ridging remains on tap for Tuesday into Wednesday with\nmuch quieter weather forecast. An upper level low looks to pass \njust to the north of NM Wed aftn through Thur morning. This system\nmay bring light showers to northern NM, but no impacts are \nexpected. Another backdoor cold front will slide down the plains \nThursday bringing a few light breezes to the area, otherwise quiet\nconditions will prevail. Models continue to indicate a trough \nwill cross NM around the Friday/Saturday timeframe, but most \nmodels suggest this will be mainly a dry passage.",
